{"id": 74, "ts": 1780774330.6577544, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate the emphasis you placed on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress handling and technical aptitude, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger overall fit.\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, proven calmness in crisis, and ability to make correct decisions quickly address the core safety\u2011critical criteria of operational reliability, stress resilience, and decision quality.\u202fHis strong sense of responsibility and deep technical understanding (\u201cunderstands complicated technology\u201d) further reinforce his suitability for the complex, data\u2011driven environment of long\u2011distance flights.\nIn contrast, B\u2019s interpersonal shortcomings\u2014being grumpy, uncooperative, pretentious, and making nasty remarks\u2014directly jeopardize crew cooperation and professional communication, which are essential in a multi\u2011crew cockpit. Moreover, his weak memory for numbers raises concerns about attention to detail and information accuracy, a risk we cannot overlook. While C\u2019s communication style is described as difficult and he appears egocentric, the evidence also shows he creates a positive crew atmosphere, suggesting he can still function effectively within the team. His limited willingness for further education is a development point, but it is more remediable through training than the fundamental safety risks posed by B\u2019s attitude and memory issues.\nTherefore, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall match for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
